<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#chain-mail">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chain mail</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as chain-mail</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chain mail is armour made of small interlocking metal rings. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, some <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> fielded armoured horsemen equipped in a tradition of quilted and chain-mail armour long characteristic of Sudanic warfare. Such cavalry was effective against regional rivals but not against British firearms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chain-mail.jpg" alt="Chain mail" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Metropolitan Museum of Art · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mail_Shirt_MET_DP147153.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
